patch 345 -- FUN_1000_11e0: reconstruct the MEMMGR object-pool init (signature-preserving, pools built).

The MEMMGR object-pool init (asm 0x111e0) builds two 2-node sentinel lists in a pool struct, each node
unlinked from the free-node list (DGROUP:0x16e2 head / 0x16dc count) by FUN_1000_1099 (asm 0x11099) which
RETURNS the node segment IN DS -- the field stores then run with DS=that node.  Ghidra dropped the DS
reassignment, so every field store landed at DGROUP:0..0xe (DAT_1000_c000..c00e), which (a) never built
the pools and (b) node-B's [0]=0xffff CLOBBERED the engine signature 0xcbc3 at DGROUP:0 (so the SOUNDDVR
init `cmpw [ds:0],0xcbc3`, drv asm 0x94, failed -> device registration skipped) and (c) overwrote the near
reloc-applier service vectors at DGROUP:0x0a/0x0e (f7ef/f81d), accidentally suppressing the 5 near-applier
sites.  Reconstruct 11e0 faithfully with an inline node-alloc (mirrors 1099 exactly, leaving the shared
base-lost 1099 untouched -- it is called from ~17 sites and is resolved per-caller), writing every field to
the REAL node segment; the signature + service vectors at DGROUP:0..0xe are preserved.  Un-suppressing the
near appliers is completed by patch 346 (which threads the 5 sites via the loader shim); the two land
together.  Asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0x111e0..0x11295 (node-alloc 0x11099).
